review_comments.body:
**Bug:** this recurses whenever the *source* value is an object, even when the target value isn't one. In that case the recursive call hits the `!target.is_object()` early return and returns the target unchanged, so `diff` becomes e.g. `[]`, `""`, or `0`. `basic_json::empty()` is `true` for an empty array (and for `null`), so the change is dropped:

```
merge_diff({"a":{"x":1}}, {"a":[]})  ->  {}      // should be {"a":[]}
merge_diff({"a":{}},      {"a":[]})  ->  {}      // should be {"a":[]}
```

As @cschreib-ibex suggested earlier, only recurse when both sides are objects:

```cpp
if (it.value().is_object() && itf.value().is_object())
{
    auto diff = merge_diff(it.value(), itf.value());
    if (!diff.empty())
    {
        result[it.key()] = std::move(diff);
    }
}
else if (it.value() != itf.value())
{
    result[it.key()] = itf.value();
}
```

